nodecode-office is a rewrite of DECRUX9812's DECRUX9812/hermes-office:

  https://github.com/DECRUX9812/hermes-office
  commit b53630cd0f0edc10645d63899a5a2515f8015fc5
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 DECRUX9812 and hermes-office contributors (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the five verbs, in Common Lisp and without Python. hermes-office edits Word,
PowerPoint and Excel through the paper-docx, paper-pptx and paper-xlsx forks; this cell reads
the same OOXML parts directly as ZIP entries and XML text, so an edit is a string change on one
part and a repack. Kept are what a user of the original gets: the same tools for the same
files, a write confined to folders the operator puts on a desk, a byte-exact backup and a
revertible receipt for every write, and Word edits left as tracked changes (w:del + w:ins)
carrying an author.

Left out, because the rewrite is a cell and not a desktop application: the Desk page and its
workstreams, before/after previews and diffs, comment threading, accept/reject of revisions
already in a document, PowerPoint deck composition and diff, Excel cell and formula writes,
and the LibreOffice recalculation step (so no external program is run at all). An edit also
matches inside one formatting run in this rewrite, where the original's libraries matched
across runs; the tool says so when it does not find its phrase.
